---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
import { JOURNEY, OPEN_QUESTIONS, PINK_APTITUDES, SCHOOL_WORK, NYUCHI_WORK } from '../data/origins.js';

const PRESENTATION_URL = 'https://origins-with-perspective.nyuchi.workers.dev';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Origins with a Perspective on Human Potential"
  description="Equity and the assumptions we make in learning — what growing up in Zimbabwe taught me about measuring capability instead of credentials, and how that shapes the technology work I do now."
  path="/origins-with-perspective"
  sheet="03 / 04"
  ogType="article"
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Sheet 03 · Off the bench"
    title="Origins with a Perspective on Human Potential"
    lede="Equity: the assumptions we make in learning. Where I came from, where education itself began, and the gap between what we say we value and what we actually measure."
    note="questions, not answers"
  >
    <p class="header-actions">
      <a class="btn" href={PRESENTATION_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Open the presentation
      </a>
    </p>
  </PageHeader>

  <!-- Why -->
  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow is-open">Why this exists</p>
    <h2 class="section-title sheet-h2" id="why-heading">The lens I bring</h2>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I work in technology at an international school. Most of my colleagues know me as the person
        who fixes things, rolls out systems, and lately introduces AI tools. That is a fair
        description of the job. It is not a complete description of the lens I bring to it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am from Zimbabwe — for a long stretch, the only person on my team who is a citizen of a
        country outside the first world. Growing up there in the nineties and two-thousands taught me
        something that has never left me: <em
          >skills meant survival and success, not grades or the name of a good school.</em
        > When infrastructure fails on a schedule, when the problems in front of you are not in any textbook,
        when innovation is the difference between thriving and merely getting by, you end up with a different
        working definition of intelligence.
      </p>
      <p>
        So when our school turned its equity lens on the assumptions we make about students, I wanted
        to bring that definition into the room. Not as a critique — as a question I genuinely cannot
        answer alone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The argument -->
  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="argument-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow is-open">The argument</p>
    <h2 class="section-title sheet-h2" id="argument-heading">Capability over credentials</h2>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        In Zimbabwe, you succeeded on what you could actually do — adapt, collaborate, solve the
        unexpected — rather than by following the well-lit path of good grades to good college to
        good job. Capability mattered more than credentials, because credentials alone did not keep
        the lights on.
      </p>
      <p>
        That made me curious about education&rsquo;s own origins. The great centres of learning, from
        Alexandria to the Renaissance academies, evaluated scholars on their ability to contribute
        new knowledge, argue well, and solve genuinely hard problems. Not on recall under artificial
        time pressure.
      </p>
    </div>

    <blockquote class="pull">
      When did we shift from cultivating intellectual excellence to measuring test-taking ability?
    </blockquote>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Here is the tension I keep running into in my own work: I am helping introduce technologies
        that handle information recall instantly, while we still often assess students on their
        ability to memorise information under time pressure. Both things are true at once, and I do
        not think we have fully reckoned with that.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Journey -->
  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="journey-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow is-open">The path here</p>
    <h2 class="section-title sheet-h2" id="journey-heading">How I got here</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Zimbabwe to South Africa to Japan to Singapore. Classroom to server room to strategy — which is
      why I keep asking questions that sit awkwardly between all three.
    </p>

    <ol class="journey">
      {
        JOURNEY.map((stop) => (
          <li class="journey__item" style={`--stop-mineral: var(--mineral-${stop.mineral})`}>
            <p class="journey__meta">
              {stop.period} &middot; {stop.place}
            </p>
            <h3 class="journey__title">{stop.title}</h3>
            <p class="journey__body">{stop.detail}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- Current work -->
  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="now-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow is-open">Now</p>
    <h2 class="section-title sheet-h2" id="now-heading">What I&rsquo;m working on</h2>
    <p class="lede">Two halves of the same question — one inside a school, one across a continent.</p>

    <div class="columns">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow is-open">Singapore American School</p>
        <ul class="work-list">
          {
            SCHOOL_WORK.map((item) => (
              <Panel as="li" style={`--item-mineral: var(--mineral-${item.mineral})`}>
                <h3>{item.title}</h3>
                <p>{item.detail}</p>
              </Panel>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow is-open">Nyuchi Africa</p>
        <ul class="work-list">
          {
            NYUCHI_WORK.map((item) => (
              <Panel as="li" style={`--item-mineral: var(--mineral-${item.mineral})`}>
                <h3>
                  {item.href ? (
                    <a href={item.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                      {item.title}
                    </a>
                  ) : (
                    item.title
                  )}
                </h3>
                <p>{item.detail}</p>
              </Panel>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <Panel as="div" class="aside"><p>
      The Nyuchi work was built for places where credentials were never the thing that got you
      through. That is the same instinct I bring to the work at school.
    </p></Panel>
  </section>

  <!-- Conceptual age -->
  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="pink-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow is-open">The Conceptual Age</p>
    <h2 class="section-title sheet-h2" id="pink-heading">Six aptitudes</h2>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Daniel Pink&rsquo;s <a
          href="https://www.danpink.com/books/whole-new-mind/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">A Whole New Mind</a
        > argues that abundance, automation and Asia have moved the premium away from logical, linear,
        spreadsheet work and toward what he calls high concept and high touch — the abilities that are
        hard to outsource and hard to automate.
      </p>
      <p>
        What struck me reading it is that these are the skills that drove success in Zimbabwe out of
        necessity. The Conceptual Age is not a forecast for me. It is a description of where I grew
        up.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="aptitudes">
      {
        PINK_APTITUDES.map((aptitude) => (
          <Panel as="li" style={`--aptitude-mineral: var(--mineral-${aptitude.mineral})`}>
            <h3>{aptitude.name}</h3>
            <p>{aptitude.detail}</p>
          </Panel>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Questions -->
  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="questions-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow is-open">Open</p>
    <h2 class="section-title sheet-h2" id="questions-heading">The questions that matter</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      I don&rsquo;t have answers — just questions from someone seeing the work through a different
      lens.
    </p>

    <ul class="questions">
      {
        OPEN_QUESTIONS.map((question) => (
          <Panel as="li" style={`--question-mineral: var(--mineral-${question.mineral})`}>
            <h3>{question.title}</h3>
            <p>{question.body}</p>
          </Panel>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <blockquote class="pull">
      Are there brilliant minds we&rsquo;re missing because we&rsquo;re measuring the wrong things?
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <!-- Presentation -->
  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="deck-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow is-open">The deck</p>
    <h2 class="section-title sheet-h2" id="deck-heading">The presentation</h2>
    <p class="lede">The original scrolling deck, as it was delivered. It reads best full screen.</p>

    <Panel as="div" class="deck">
      <iframe
        src={PRESENTATION_URL}
        title="Origins with a Perspective on Human Potential — presentation"
        loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </Panel>

    <p class="header-actions">
      <a class="btn" href={PRESENTATION_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Open full screen
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section reveal" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
    <h2 class="section-title sheet-h2" id="cta-heading">What have you noticed?</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      If you work in education, assessment, or anywhere the gap between capability and credentials
      shows up — I&rsquo;d like to hear how it looks from where you sit.
    </p>
    <p class="header-actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/book">Book a call</a>
      <a class="button is-ghost" href="mailto:bryan@nyuchi.com">bryan@nyuchi.com</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sheet-h2 {
    margin-block: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .header-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
  }


  .prose {
    max-width: 44rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink-body);
  }

  .prose em {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .pull {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-block: 2.5rem;
    padding-inline-start: 1.5rem;
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--mineral-gold);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 1.2vw, 1.625rem);
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* --- journey --- */

  .journey {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-block-start: 2.5rem;
  }

  .journey__item {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 2.25rem 2rem;
    border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .journey__item:last-child {
    padding-block-end: 0;
    border-inline-start-color: transparent;
  }

  .journey__item::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: -5px;
    inset-block-start: 0.35rem;
    width: 9px;
    height: 9px;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: var(--stop-mineral);
  }

  .journey__meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .journey__title {
    margin-block: 0.35rem 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  .journey__body {
    max-width: 42rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--ink-body);
  }

  /* --- columns --- */

  .columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(20rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem;
    margin-block-start: 2.5rem;
  }

  .work-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-block-start: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .work-list li {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--item-mineral);
  }

  .work-list h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-block-end: 0.25rem;
  }

  /*
   * These are standalone heading links, not links inside a sentence, so the
   * WCAG 2.2 target-size inline exception does not apply — they carry the
   * full 44px target.
   */
  .work-list h3 a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
  }

  .work-list h3 a:hover {
    color: var(--item-mineral);
  }

  .work-list p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-body);
  }

  .aside {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-block-start: 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--ink-body);
  }

  /* --- aptitudes & questions --- */

  .aptitudes,
  .questions {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(16rem, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-block-start: 2rem;
  }

  .aptitudes li,
  .questions li {
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 0;
  }

  .aptitudes h3,
  .questions h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-block-end: 0.35rem;
  }

  .aptitudes h3 {
    color: var(--aptitude-mineral);
  }

  .questions h3 {
    color: var(--question-mineral);
  }

  .aptitudes p,
  .questions p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-body);
  }

  /* --- deck --- */

  .deck {
    margin-block-start: 2rem;
    border-radius: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .deck iframe {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: min(70dvh, 40rem);
    min-height: 30rem;
    border: 0;
  }
</style>
